[size=6][b]Get Out of the Way — NPCs step aside naturally in SpaceBourne 2[/b][/size]

In SpaceBourne 2's stations, markets and corridors, people stand in your way: you stop, or you shove them aside with your body. With Get Out of the Way, calm NPCs notice you walking at them, turn, take a short step out of your path, and step back to their spot once you have passed.

Version 0.1.2 · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/14]Nexus Mods page[/url] · UE4SS Lua mod · works alone or with the rest of the [url=#part-of-the-spacebourne-2-realism-set]realism set[/url].

[line]
[size=5][b]What it does[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Who steps aside:[/b] civilians, guards at rest, allied crew and companions, your ground squad, and the traders, quest givers and crew you talk to.
[*][b]Who never does:[/b] enemies, creatures, bosses, anyone in a fight or alerted, anyone talking to you, sitting, playing a scripted animation or already walking somewhere.
[*][b]Natural:[/b] the NPC walks its step with its own walk animation and turns the way it goes. It steps to the side it is already on, a little away from you, 0.5 to 0.8 m, just enough to clear your path. It never steps into a wall or into another NPC: if one side is blocked it takes the other, and if both are blocked it stays.
[*][b]Back to its spot:[/b] once you have passed, it walks back and ends where it stood, facing the same way.
[*][b]Human timing:[/b] it reacts within 0.2–0.4 s when you are about 2 m away (further when you run), and also when you are already pressed against it and keep pushing. Someone with their back to you notices later, and doesn't notice at all if you sneak up crouched.
[*][b]Calm, not twitchy:[/b] at most 4 NPCs move at once, and the same NPC waits 3 s before it steps again.
[*][b]Out of the way of the fights:[/b] nothing happens while you are in a ship or on the hoverbike, or while Silent Ops reports an alert of Yellow or higher near you.
[*][b]On by default.[/b] No key needed.
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]SpaceBourne 2 (Steam).
[*][url=https://github.com/UE4SS-RE/RE-UE4SS/releases/tag/v3.0.1]UE4SS 3.0.1[/url]. Installing HTR or the realism set installer installs it too.
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]Install[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Download GetOutOfTheWay-0.1.2.zip from the [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-GetOutOfTheWay/releases]releases[/url].
[*]Extract it into the game folder (...\steamapps\common\SpaceBourne 2\). It adds SB2\Binaries\Win64\Mods\GetOutOfTheWay\; the enabled.txt inside turns it on.
[*]That's it: walk into a station or a market.
[/list]

Manual install: copy the GetOutOfTheWay folder from this repository into SpaceBourne 2\SB2\Binaries\Win64\Mods\.

Uninstall: delete SB2\Binaries\Win64\Mods\GetOutOfTheWay. Get Out of the Way never writes to your saves.

[line]
[size=5][b]Settings[/b][/size]

Edit Mods\GetOutOfTheWay\scripts\config.lua, then restart the game. Every line is optional.

[list]
[*]Enabled: false switches the mod off completely.
[*]TriggerDistance (2.2 m): how far ahead an NPC on your path reacts (more when you run).
[*]StepDistance (0.8 m): the longest side step (0.5–1.0).
[*]PathWidth (0.75 m): how close to your line counts as "in your way".
[*]ReturnToSpot: step back to the old spot once you have passed (true).
[*]Cooldown (3 s): before the same NPC steps aside again.
[*]Who: Civilians, Guards, Allies, Squad, Talkers (true / false).
[*]ToggleKey: none by default. Set one to switch the mod on and off in game. The set's mods already use every laptop key, so pick one your own setup leaves free; the game's own keys and the other set mods' keys are refused.
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]How it works[/b][/size]

The game creates its NPCs; the mod notes the calm kinds as they appear (no searching through the world). A few times a second it looks only at the NPCs within 8 m of you: if one is ahead of you and close to your line, its own AI is told to walk to a free spot beside it, checked on the game's navigation mesh first. Details: [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-GetOutOfTheWay/blob/mainDESIGN.md]DESIGN.md[/url].

[line]
[size=5][b]Status and known limits[/b][/size]

Known limits:

[list]
[*][b]Animated decor stays put.[/b] Many station extras (people sitting at the bar, vendors behind a counter, sweepers) are animations placed in the level, not characters: they cannot walk.
[*][b]NPCs already walking keep their route.[/b] Their own AI would cancel a step at once; they go around you the game's way.
[*][b]City crowds on planets[/b] use their own simple mover and are not affected.
[*][b]If you stop on its spot[/b], the NPC waits a while and then stays where it is.
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]Part of the SpaceBourne 2 realism set[/b][/size]

This mod is part of the realism set, built around [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/4]Hardcore Tactical Realism[/url] as the core mod. HTR is not required: this mod works on its own or with any of the others. [b]Install them all at once[/b] with the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/11]SpaceBourne 2 Realism installer[/url] ([url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-Realism]GitHub[/url]): tick the mods you want, and it switches them on and keeps them up to date.

[list]
[*][b]Hardcore Tactical Realism (HTR)[/b]: the core: realistic ballistics, wounds and tactical AI. [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-HardcoreTacticalRealism]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/4]Nexus[/url] · [url=https://steamcommunity.com/app/1646850/discussions/0/573805072991123580/]Steam[/url]
[*][b]Split Controls[/b]: separate look inversion for ships and on foot. [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-SplitControls]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/5]Nexus[/url]
[*][b]Silent Ops[/b]: realistic stealth, suppressors and silent takedowns. [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-SilentOps]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/6]Nexus[/url]
[*][b]Gear Without Levels[/b]: any weapon or suit at any level, with small penalties. [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-GearWithoutLevels]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/7]Nexus[/url]
[*][b]SB2 HOTAS[/b]: joystick, HOTAS, pedals, head tracking and triple screen. [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-HOTAS]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/8]Nexus[/url]
[*][b]Faction Power[/b]: dungeons, sales and missions earn your faction power. [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-FactionPower]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/9]Nexus[/url]
[*][b]Tactical Engineering[/b]: deployable turrets and barricades that take time to set up. [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-TacticalEngineering]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/10]Nexus[/url]
[*][b]Ammo Discipline[/b]: realistic ammo limits and scavenging. [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-AmmoDiscipline]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/12]Nexus[/url]
[*][b]Ground Waypoints[/b]: planet waypoints on foot and on the hoverbike. [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-GroundWaypoints]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/13]Nexus[/url]
[*][b]Get Out of the Way[/b] [i](this mod)[/i]: NPCs step aside naturally when you walk through them. [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-GetOutOfTheWay]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/14]Nexus[/url]
[/list]

Coming soon: Tactical First Person.

